vignettes/formula-grammar.Rmd:129:| `animal(1 | id, pedigree = pedigree)`, `animal(1 | id, A = A)`, or `animal(1 | id, Ainv = Ainv)` in `mu` and/or `sigma` | Implemented first slice | Univariate Gaussian animal-model random intercept from a dense pedigree-derived additive relationship matrix, precomputed additive relatedness, or inverse-relatedness matrix. Matching `mu`/`sigma` terms estimate one latent structured correlation. One numeric `mu` slope is fitted; the exact A-matrix q1 `sigma` one-slope route is also fitted and inference-ready with caveats under raw log-SD Wald-z intervals. Native Bernoulli and non-inflated Poisson `mu` q1 supplied-`A` intercepts also support predictor-dependent SDs using `sd(id, level = "animal") ~ z`; each is a separate point-recovery/output slice. Logit Binomial adds one animal slope-only SD route via supplied `A`; the development Julia bridge passes same-data recovery and marginal-simulation checks. Native Binomial also admits one IID intercept alongside the animal slope when both have matching SD formulas. Native Beta supports the q1 animal `mu` intercept for pedigree, supplied `A`, or supplied `Ainv` at point-recovery grade, with unobserved founders permitted and group predictions returned for observed animals. The Julia bridge now has same-data Binomial/TMB point parity for one q1 animal-intercept SD route with labeled `A` or `Ainv`, and same-engine equivalence for the two matrix inputs; this does not establish broad parity or interval calibration. General pedigree/Ainv bridge marshalling, sparse large-pedigree construction, additional multiple or labelled structured-slope layouts outside the fitted forms described here, structured slope correlations, predictor-dependent `corpair()`, and other animal direct-SD routes remain planned. |
