docs/design/01-formula-grammar.md:177:| `y ~ x1 + (1 + x1 | id)`, `sigma ~ 1`, `family = lognormal()` | Implemented ML-Laplace point-fit recovery | One complete-data ordinary lognormal log-location model estimates an unlabelled intercept-slope covariance block. The recovered estimands are `sd0`, `sd1`, and group-level `rho_re` (never residual `rho12`) under the design-17 map `ρ = 0.999999 tanh(η)`, the same report symbols as Poisson (`eta_cor_mu`, `rho_mu_re`; no `logsech_mu_re`). Ledger cell `mc-0720` is `point_fit_recovery` for this exact route; it is not the independent-slope cell `mc-0380` and not Wave 2.5 NB2 `mc-0719`. The slope predictor must vary within at least one group; a predictor that is constant within every group is rejected before the fit because `sd1` and `rho_re` are unidentified. Gamma neighbour, REML, missing-response, labels, mixed `(1 \| g) + (1 + x \| g)`, structured ordinary correlated, intervals, coverage, and `supported` remain unsupported. |
